The Lord of the Abyss (Primordial Deity of Chaos)
The Lord of the Abyss, chaotic flowing mane of midnight-black strands moving as if submerged in deep water reaching shoulder blades occasionally flickering into wisps of dark flame, two swirling whirlpools of chaotic violet energy lacking pupils with trails of black smoke constantly leaking from corners, razor-sharp sunken jawline with high hollowed cheekbones pulled into perpetually predatory expression, deep obsidian charcoal skin with matte texture absorbing all light rather than reflecting, imposing unsettling height of 215 cm with Living Shadow composition that is lean elongated and possessing terrifying fluid grace, Dread-Iron plate armor as jagged asymmetrical carapaces looking like they grew naturally from his flesh with dark iridescent metal breastplate featuring central glowing Eye of the Void pulsing deep-purple, massive sharp pauldrons resembling curved demon horns dripping with thick viscous black ichor, heavy tattered Abyssal Silk mantle of smoke-captured fabric split into multiple serrated ends fluttering with life of their own, high spiked gorget forcing chin up in eternal arrogance, articulated clawed gauntlets with fingers tapering into sharp obsidian points capable of tearing space, heavy tasset of interlocking dragon-scale plates guarding hips and thighs etched with forbidden Shadow Abyss runes glowing faint magenta, form-fitting dark bruised-purple tactical trousers, massive knee-high greaves ending in sharp wing-like protrusions at sides, heavy pointed sabatons that sink into ground leaving cracked scorched footprints filled with bubbling purple energy. His weapon is the Scepter of Eternal Night, a seven-foot massive polearm with shaft of twisted petrified primordial beast bone wrapped in cold silver chains that rattle with ghostly sound, the head a jagged curved dark crystal blade housing a swirling vortex of Abyssal energy at its center, carrying a suffocating Presence of Dread as thick hazy purple-and-black miasma smelling of ancient sulfur and cold metal that expands into a massive multi-eyed shadowy god silhouette behind him.

Kael, The Reincarnation of the Lord of the Abyss
Kael, jet-black hair thick and straight falling over forehead in heavy fringe nearly covering his eyes with longer layers at back brushing shoulders typically tied back with black ribbon though persistent strands always escape to frame his face, deep violet-grey eyes large and solemn with intensity that seems to look through people glowing faint violet in low light, long narrow face with high sharp cheekbones catching light at harsh angles and straight aristocratic nose and defined strong jawline softened by lingering traces of youth rounding his chin slightly, pale cool ashen skin with dark circles beneath eyes making him look perpetually tired, dark straight eyebrows often drawn together in concentration or concern, lean and wiry physique at 175 cm with quiet coiled stillness of predator at rest and economical movement with no wasted gestures moving like someone who does not want to be noticed with footsteps light and presence fading into background, high-collared charcoal-grey wool tunic with long sleeves, black leather vest with silver buckles, simple leather cord around neck holding small dark grey smooth cold unadorned river stone keepsake from his mother, form-fitting black trousers, scuffed black boots that have seen many miles. His weapon is a pair of twin jagged sickles forged from abyssal ore each blade deep violet-black with crimson edge highlights and constant wisp of dark smoke trailing from edge measuring approximately 60 cm along curve with grips wrapped in black leather and bone and pommels shaped like miniature screaming skulls with hollow eye sockets glowing faintly red, carrying an aura of Protective Shadow as subtle pull on surrounding darkness that deepens when he is anxious with temperature drop and flickering lights, his shadows being the quiet darkness of a moonless night that offers rest and hiding rather than consuming souls.

