[Beast of Abyss]

Malakar (Human Form)
Malakar, a sharply handsome yet sinister face with a razor-edged jawline and high, cruel cheekbones, a straight narrow nose, thin lips often curled into a cold, knowing smirk, piercing crimson-red eyes with vertical slit pupils that glow faintly in darkness, dark eyebrows arched with mocking confidence, flawless pale skin with an ashen undertone, two small obsidian-black horns curving back from the temples through a wild mane of jet-black hair swept upward and backward in chaotic spiked layers with streaks of deep violet, no helmet, a lean powerful upper body with broad shoulders and a narrow waist, visible dark vein-like markings crawling up the sides of the neck, a fitted high-collared longcoat of midnight black leather with jagged asymmetrical cuts over a deep burgundy inner lining, the collar flared and lined with black fur, a pauldron of jagged dark iron shaped like a snarling dragon skull on the left shoulder, a ribcage-like harness of matte black straps and silver buckles across the chest, right arm wrapped in bandages from elbow to knuckles under a clawed gauntlet of blackened steel with glowing violet fissures, left arm bare from the bicep down with abyssal runes etched into the skin that pulse with a dim purple light, tight charcoal-grey combat trousers with reinforced padding at the thighs, a heavy belt of black iron chains and a central buckle shaped like a fanged maw with a glowing crimson gem, multiple dark chains hanging diagonally across the hips, black leather boots rising to just below the knee with pointed steel toe-caps and jagged silver plating along the shins, the heels adorned with small curved obsidian spikes, twin weapons that are massive jagged sickles forged from abyssal ore, each blade a deep violet-black with crimson edge highlights and a constant wisp of dark smoke, the grips wrapped in black leather and bone, the pommels shaped like miniature screaming skulls with hollow eye sockets glowing red, and a constant subtle aura of encroaching shadow and faint whispers.

Malakar (Beast Form)
Malakar in Beast form, a colossal quadrupedal abyssal dragon-beast with a body frame similar to the Sacred Beast but twisted by darkness, a massive draconic-leonine head with a blunt armored snout covered in jagged black metal plating, six glowing malevolent violet eyes arranged in two vertical rows, four massive ridged horns of obsidian black curling backward and downward with inner veins of molten crimson, a thick mane of shadowy ethereal black fur crackling with purple static electricity cascading down the neck, dark indigo skin stretched over a heavily muscled upper body with a deep barrel chest, pulsing crimson vein-like light-marks wrapping the forelimbs and thighs, a pair of enormous leathery dragon wings sprouting from the shoulders, the wing membranes a tattered deep violet-black stretched between elongated bone-like digits tipped with hooked claws, the wings constantly dripping wisps of dark smoke, a spine of jagged black spikes running from the crown of the head down to the tail tip, the lower body robust and supported by four powerful legs ending in massive black-clawed paws with cracked golden shackles embedded in the ankles, a long whip-like tail ending in a cluster of serrated bone blades that rattle when swung, integrated dark iron plating on the forepaws like gauntlets, primary weapons being colossal jagged claws that glow with sickly purple flame and a maw filled with rows of needle-like black teeth, a corrupt abyssal aura radiating from the body in waves of deep purple and black that distort the air and cause the ground to decay, occasional bolts of red-black lightning arcing between the horns and wing tips, the entire form a living embodiment of the Abyss.